   {
    "text": "The first brick keeper's cottage at Cape Florida was finished in 1825.",
    "url": "https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=80255"
   },
   {
    "text": "Burned in an 1836 Seminole attack, the cottage was rebuilt under Reason Duke and completed in 1846.",
    "url": "https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=80255"
   },
   {
    "text": "Six families of lighthouse keepers lived in the cottage in turn until 1878.",
    "url": "https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=80255"
   },
   {
    "text": "The State of Florida built the current replica of the keeper's quarters in 1969.",
    "url": "https://www.hmdb.org/m.asp?m=80255"
   }
